            <ArticleTitle>[Acute evolution as a rare complication of a chronic calcified pancreatitis. Report of a Malagasy case (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Report of an acute inflammatory syndrome of the right side of the belly with fever, polyleucocytosis and diabetes in a 35 years old patient with chronic calcified pancreatitis. The right colon was moved forward by an important retroperitoneal infiltration and the pathology demonstrated a cytosteatonecrosis. The post-operative period was disturbed by hyperamylasemia, hyperamylasuria and an external pancreatic fistule.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
